sophia: Quick sync — I want to open a docs PR that contains a compact, end-to-end troubleshooting example showing graceful fallback from a full-context request to a trimmed prompt, plus how to handle 429s and timeouts. Plan: include both JS and Python SDK snippets, a short migration note for older SDKs, and a perf caveat. Any blockers?

alex: I can own the JS example. My idea: show a single helper that attempts the full prompt, and on 429/timeouts performs an exponential backoff and then trims the oldest user messages (preserve system + assistant).

kevin: Agree with approach. Small Q: should we prefer `Retry-After` from server responses when present, or always do exponential backoff+jitter? Our responses expose `retry-after` sometimes. Need a docs link to the exact header semantics. I couldn’t find the current anchor quickly.

maria: We moved the retry header section into errors/reference during the last docs reshuffle. I can add a crosslink from the troubleshooting guide to that anchor. Also, note: the new Python SDK exposes `sdk.trim_context()` helper — we should surface that in the Python snippet so users don't implement trimming incorrectly.

ryan: FYI from eng-ml: add a perf note. Trimming aggressively can actually increase per-request latency because the model loses cached KV state and recomputes. Suggest we add a recommended heuristic: try trimming 15-25% first, then incremental trims with a hard lower bound. Also mention token budgeting.

alex: Draft JS snippet below — feel free to shorten for docs.
```js
// JS: try full context, on 429/timeouts backoff then trim oldest user messages and retry
async function generateWithFallback(client, messages) {
  let attempt = 0;
  while (attempt < 3) {
    try {
      return await client.chat.completions.create({ model: 'redwood-2', messages });
    } catch (err) {
      attempt += 1;
      const is429 = err.statusCode === 429;
      const isTimeout = err.code === 'ETIMEDOUT' || err.name === 'TimeoutError';
      if (!is429 && !isTimeout) throw err;
      const ra = err.headers && err.headers['retry-after'] ? parseInt(err.headers['retry-after']) * 1000 : null;
      const backoff = ra ?? Math.min(1000 * 2 ** attempt, 5000);
      await new Promise(res => setTimeout(res, backoff + Math.floor(Math.random() * 300)));
      // trim oldest 20% of user messages (keep system and assistant)
      messages = trimOldestUserMessages(messages, 0.2);
    }
  }
  throw new Error('all retries failed');
}
```

